<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10260" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπαρ-άγω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾱγ</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shift in order to meet attacks,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς σάκκους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					3.7.20
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be shifted in the other direction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be produced correspondingly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				2.4.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>adduce, allege on the other side,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.719c
			</span></i>: abs., <i>argue on the other side,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.267S.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Vit.</u>
				p.4J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> more freq. intr.,
				<i>lead an army against, advance to meet the enemy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.6.43
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>march parallel with, skirt,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς ὑπωρείαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.77.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				3.53.4
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
